-- A constructor re-exported by the single-name form `export import m.Tz`.
--
-- facade carries m's type `Tz` and, because the name also spells m's constructor,
-- the constructor `Tz` too: resolve binds `Tz` here to m's arity-1 constructor, and
-- `check` and `run` agree.  The emitted program must name the same constructor, so
-- the ctor-export index (`types/private_mangle.ctorExportsFrom`) has to carry the
-- single-name hop as the export surface does.
--
-- Expected output, derived by hand from the semantics: `unTz (Tz 5)` = `5`.
import facade.{Tz, unTz}

main : <IO> Unit
main = putStrLn (intToString (unTz (Tz 5)))
